<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">ROADMAP · TRANSPARENT BY DEFAULT</p><h1>Earn stability one milestone at a time.</h1><p>This roadmap distinguishes implemented foundations from work that remains. Priorities may change as maintainers and contributors learn.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container roadmap">
    <article><span class="roadmap-marker done">✓</span><div><span class="status status-implemented">Foundation present</span><h2>Core application lifecycle</h2><p>Bootstrap, routing, middleware, configuration, validation, views, logging, CLI, and PDO/migration building blocks are implemented with tests. Live MySQL verification remains environment-dependent.</p></div></article>
    <article><span class="roadmap-marker active">02</span><div><span class="status status-experimental">In progress</span><h2>Release verification and security defaults</h2><p>Keep authorization explicit, run reproducible quality checks, test browser flows, document limitations, and establish maintainable release practices before claiming stability.</p></div></article>
    <article><span class="roadmap-marker planned">03</span><div><span class="status status-planned">Planned</span><h2>Production deployment guidance</h2><p>Document supported server setups, operational limits, secure configuration, observability, and real deployment examples without treating the development server as production-ready.</p></div></article>
    <article><span class="roadmap-marker planned">04</span><div><span class="status status-planned">Planned</span><h2>Stable extension points</h2><p>Review and version public APIs, improve developer guides and API references, and define backward-compatibility policy as the project matures.</p></div></article>
    <article><span class="roadmap-marker planned">05</span><div><span class="status status-planned">Planned</span><h2>Optional AI integration layer</h2><p>After the framework foundation is reliable: provider interfaces, a controlled tool registry, validated arguments, permission checks, and auditable execution.</p></div></article>
    <article><span class="roadmap-marker planned">06</span><div><span class="status status-planned">Planned</span><h2>Community and localization</h2><p>Develop French and Arabic documentation, grow public contribution workflows, and investigate Moroccan PHP projects before making comparative claims.</p></div></article>
</div></section>
